From 8e262f302c977cc5e603439cdee58d5b83ce6bc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:54:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: rkisp2: Add support for the RV1126 ISP

The RV1126 ISP is version 2.0 of the hardware that this driver supports
on the RK3588. The register layout is the same for the blocks that the
driver configures. It has three clocks, a third interrupt line for the
CSI-2 receiver and memory read status, and 4416x3312 as maximum input
size.

Add the RV1126 model description and a handler for the third interrupt,
which counts the receiver errors. The ISP 2.0 differs from the RK3588
variant in a few places that the model description carries:

 - the image stabiliser is gone, so its output crop is not programmed;
 - the bus priorities and hurry modes come from the upper bits of the
   ISP control register;
 - the memory interface read and raw read clocks are gated by bits 21
   and 22 of VI_ISP_CLK_CTRL, which have to be set;
 - a raw readback delivers the last lines of a Bayer to YUV frame only
   when the readback presents extra lines, which the readback buffer
   size, the picture size and the ISP window include;
 - the raw readback samples are not word swapped;
 - the readback buffer is returned at the ISP frame complete interrupt,
   when the whole frame has been read;
 - the soft reset pulse of the ISP does not clear the readback front
   end, so the stop path asserts the "isp" and "isp-rx-p" resets.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
